cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gazeCOM in research, software, or artistic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "gazeCOM"
abstract: >-
  gazeCOM is an open-source system for saliency-driven iterative image
  generation and composition. It introduces a point-centered method for image
  extension: instead of specifying a boundary to which an image should be
  outpainted, it defines a point of interest and generates a fixed-size crop
  around that coordinate. The same coordinate anchors the result's placement
  in a persistent composite. Human input, algorithmic movement, and computer
  vision provide interchangeable ways to select the point. The VLM Guide adds
  model-selected placement, prompt decisions, and bounded visual memory on top
  of this coordinate system.
authors:
  - name: "grebenshyo"
